 3, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-28T22:46:12.152Z", "request_id": "req_011CgVSr6Ek9jFCDUynTGDC1", "thinking_duration_ms": 43358}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_stop", "index": 0}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_start", "index": 1, "content_block": {"type": "text", "text": ""}}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011CgVSr6UtVykAS6snP5XvT", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Rough estimates (worked in my head, no simulation run):\n\n- **Fixed ordering cost.** Plans that order every day (1, 2, 7) pay 25 × 25 = 625. Plans that order every 2 days (3, 4, 5) pay 325. Plan 0 (every 3 days) pays about 225. Plan 6 (every 4 days) pays 175.\n- **Order size compared with the forecast.**\n  - Plans 2, 3 and 6 order exactly the forecast. But actual demand averages about 1.046 × forecast, so they run short regularly. A missed unit costs 10 for item 0 and 12 for item 1 (lost margin plus penalty). Holding a unit for a day costs only 0.5–0.7, so running short is the bigger loss.\n  - Plans 0, 1 and 4 order about 3–6% above forecast.\n  - Plan 5 orders about 15% above forecast.\n  - Plan 7 orders about 20% above forecast, every day.\n- **Excess stock (plan 7).** Over the whole period, plan 7 orders about 85–87 units of each item beyond expected demand. Some of that expires or is left at the end (roughly 1,100 in purchase cost), and holding adds more. Still, it almost never runs short.\n- **Plan 6.** Each delivery is about 146 units against a 148-unit warehouse, so any leftover stock makes the excess vanish on arrival. On top of that it orders exactly the forecast and carries high holding costs. It looks weak.\n- **Order cycle.** Ordering every 2–3 days with a moderate buffer looks best. Each order covers more than one day, so random swings partly cancel out, and fixed costs are lower. Plan 5 has the right buffer, plans 4 and 0 are close behind. Plans 7 and 1 are borderline. Plans 3, 2 and 6 run short too often.\n\nMy top four are plans 5, 4, 0 and 7. Plan 7 versus plan 1 is close to a coin flip, which is why plan 7 gets 0.52."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 4482, "cache_read_input_tokens": 2313, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 4482}, "output_tokens": 3, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-28T22:46:20.091Z", "request_id": "req_011CgVSr6Ek9jFCDUynTGDC1"}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_stop", "index": 1}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_start", "index": 2, "content_block": {"type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_019B3ZB9WscG1hTzpmJxmTkQ", "name": "StructuredOutput", "input": {}, "caller": {"type": "direct"}}}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011CgVSr6UtVykAS6snP5XvT", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_019B3ZB9WscG1hTzpmJxmTkQ", "name": "StructuredOutput", "input": {"p": [0.6, 0.45, 0.2, 0.4, 0.7, 0.75, 0.25, 0.52]}, "caller": {"type": "direct"}}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 4482, "cache_read_input_tokens": 2313, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 4482}, "output_tokens": 3, "service_tier": "standard", "